  "verbalization": "Sufentanil, as part of the Full Opioid Agonists class, binds to Oprm1 through a shared mechanism involving opioid receptor agonist activity. This is supported by multiple paths that link Sufentanil to Oprm1 via different opioid receptor agonist subclasses, such as Remifentanil, Dihydrocodeine, and Levorphanol. The commonality across these pathways lies in the involvement of the Opioid Receptor Agonist category, suggesting a general mechanism of action for these compounds. The presence of anilide and organonitrogen compounds as common ancestors further underscores the structural and functional overlap among these drugs. While the exact binding affinity or mechanism may vary, the shared classification and functional role in activating Oprm1 provide a cohesive explanation for their relationship.",
